                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 23 at 11:48AM EDT until September 23 at 2:45PM EDT by NWS Charleston WV",
                "description": "FFWRLX\n\nThe National Weather Service in Charleston has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSouthern Cabell County in central West Virginia...\nCentral Wayne County in western West Virginia...\n\n* Until 245 PM EDT.\n\n* At 1148 AM EDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1.5 and 2.5 inches of\nrain have fallen. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nWayne, Beech Fork State Park, Barboursville, East Lynn Lake, East\nLynn, Salt Rock, Genoa and Pea Ridge.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nReport flooding to the National Weather Service by calling toll free,\n800 401 9535, when you can do so safely.",
